WEBVTT

00:00.740 --> 00:02.730
Here's the school garden.

00:02.730 --> 00:04.550
Nadeko-chan's awesome.

00:04.550 --> 00:06.960
She can grow all sorts 
of flowers and veggies.

00:06.960 --> 00:08.320
She's got a green thumb.

00:08.320 --> 00:10.220
What was that? Tom Thumb?

00:10.220 --> 00:13.100
It's someone who's good at gardening.

00:13.100 --> 00:13.840
Tom is?

00:13.840 --> 00:14.990
No! Your thumb!

00:14.990 --> 00:15.600
Huh?

00:15.600 --> 00:18.270
You never make any sense, Akira.

00:18.270 --> 00:19.950
Is something there?

00:20.830 --> 00:21.900
Oh, that?

00:21.900 --> 00:24.420
Nadeko-chan, what's the name of this flower?

00:24.420 --> 00:27.370
Oh, it's called sweet myrtle.

00:27.370 --> 00:29.610
You can use it herbally 
or make liquor from it.

00:29.610 --> 00:31.610
Also, you can eat the berries that grow.

00:31.610 --> 00:32.470
Huh.

00:31.970 --> 00:32.790
I wanna eat some!

00:33.610 --> 00:35.790
It looks kind of like a star.

00:37.530 --> 00:38.970
I see fish.

00:38.970 --> 00:41.440
Ah, don't do that, Akira. It's dangerous.

00:41.440 --> 00:42.070
What?

00:42.070 --> 00:44.330
If you look into the eyes of 
your reflection in the river,

00:44.330 --> 00:45.950
they say you'll die in three days.

00:45.950 --> 00:46.600
Eh?!

00:46.600 --> 00:48.180
Did you lock eyes just now?

00:48.180 --> 00:50.630
I did, I think...

00:50.630 --> 00:53.340
A-Am I going to die?

00:53.340 --> 00:54.580
You think I'm going to die?

00:54.580 --> 00:57.310
Reimi-chan, that's enough fibbing.

00:57.310 --> 01:00.410
They say that so you won't 
lean over the bridge and fall.

01:01.380 --> 01:03.580
Yoka-chan, watch out!

01:04.850 --> 01:06.910
Seriously, watch out! You'll fall!

01:07.630 --> 01:10.210
Staring into your own eyes 
in the river is dangerous.

01:13.380 --> 01:14.670
Thanks.

01:15.430 --> 01:18.240
I wanna become a master of Agano jiu-jitsu

01:18.240 --> 01:19.900
and fight an anteater!

01:19.900 --> 01:21.440
I wanna become really smart!

01:21.440 --> 01:24.690
I wanna be able to eat 
all sorts of mushrooms!

01:24.690 --> 01:26.300
I totally wanna find some little people!

01:26.300 --> 01:27.850
You're amazing, Shizuru-chan.

01:27.850 --> 01:28.880
Huh, really?

01:28.880 --> 01:30.770
Aw, shucks...

01:30.770 --> 01:32.090
Hey, Shizuru-chan...

01:32.090 --> 01:32.880
Why?

01:32.880 --> 01:34.250
Why what?

01:34.250 --> 01:36.070
Why are you so amazing?

01:36.070 --> 01:37.250
Why am I amazing?

01:37.250 --> 01:37.860
Yeah.

01:37.860 --> 01:40.250
Huh, I wonder why.

01:40.250 --> 01:45.150
Cuz I do what I want, 
and I go where I want, maybe?

01:45.150 --> 01:46.580
That's amazing.

01:46.950 --> 01:48.950
I can't do anything.

01:48.950 --> 01:50.220
Then cheer me on!

01:50.220 --> 01:50.830
Huh?

01:50.830 --> 01:52.570
Sure, I'll cheer you on.

01:52.570 --> 01:54.540
I think I can do that, maybe.

01:54.540 --> 01:55.660
Me too!

01:55.660 --> 01:56.920
I'll be cheering, too.

01:56.920 --> 01:58.670
I'll cheer you on, Yoka.

01:58.670 --> 02:00.040
I'll cheer hard as I can!

02:00.040 --> 02:00.670
Me?

02:00.670 --> 02:01.330
Yeah.

02:03.710 --> 02:07.280
Let's promise on that big, 
twinkling promise star.

02:07.280 --> 02:08.660
Promise star?

02:08.660 --> 02:10.360
I just made up that name.

02:10.360 --> 02:12.910
I think its name is Sirius.

02:13.240 --> 02:16.040
Let's make that our name, then.

02:16.040 --> 02:16.860
Okay.

02:41.300 --> 02:45.060
<b>Train to the End of the World</b>

03:56.870 --> 03:59.230
How long's it been since 
we left Higashi-Agano?

03:59.230 --> 04:00.850
Two or three hours?

04:00.850 --> 04:03.400
These stations are so far apart.

04:03.400 --> 04:06.520
They used to be so close 
before the 7G incident.

04:06.790 --> 04:09.490
Why didn't I take the train more?

04:09.490 --> 04:11.790
We all took it for granted.

04:11.790 --> 04:15.510
Ikebukuro would have taken 
no time at all back then.

04:15.520 --> 04:23.650
<b>m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100</b>

04:15.520 --> 04:23.650
<b>31 Agano
30 Higashi-Agano
29 Musashi-Yokote
28 Koma
27 Higashi-Hanno
26 Hanno
25 Motokaji
24 Bushi
23 Irumashi
22 Inariyama-koen
21 Musashi-Fujisawa
20 Sayamagaoka
19 Kotesashi
18 Nishi-Tokorozawa
17 Tokorozawa
16 Akitsu
15 Kiyose
14 Higashi-Kurume
13 Hibarigaoka
12 Hoya
11 Oizumi-gakuen
10 Shakujii-koen
09 Nerima-Takanodai
08 Fujimidai
07 Nakamurabashi
06 Nerima
05 Sakuradai
04 Ekoda
03 Higashi-Nagasaki
02 Shiinamachi
01 Ikebukuro</b>

04:15.740 --> 04:19.210
It's exactly thirty stops from 
Agano to Ikebukuro Station,

04:19.210 --> 04:21.230
which means we have twenty-nine stops left.

04:21.230 --> 04:23.660
That's so far! It's gonna be a long trip.

04:21.570 --> 04:23.650
<b>Rapid Express/F Liner</b>

04:21.570 --> 04:23.650
<b>Rapid Express

Express

Commuter Express

Rapid

Commuter Semi Express

Semi Express</b>

04:23.660 --> 04:25.350
I wonder if Yoka-chan's doing okay.

04:25.350 --> 04:26.900
I'm sure she is.

04:26.900 --> 04:27.910
Think she'll be surprised?

04:27.910 --> 04:28.470
Yeah.

04:28.470 --> 04:31.240
I'm sure she'll be really 
happy to see all of us.

04:31.240 --> 04:36.290
I hope we don't end up as grandmas 
by the time we reach Ikebukuro.

04:36.290 --> 04:37.180
Wait, never mind.

04:37.180 --> 04:38.700
We'd be animals instead.

04:38.700 --> 04:40.210
Animals, huh?

04:41.270 --> 04:46.560
Didn't Matsuta-san say your lifespan gets 
cut short if those mushrooms grow on you?

04:46.560 --> 04:49.220
That you could die in as little as one year.

04:49.220 --> 04:50.730
She did say that.

04:50.730 --> 04:53.850
But you're super happy 
while you're alive, right?

04:53.850 --> 04:54.930
Yeah...

04:55.600 --> 04:57.430
What do you think, Akira?

04:57.430 --> 04:58.430
About what?

04:58.430 --> 04:59.770
I mean, for example...

04:59.770 --> 05:02.010
If you got to read super-fun books,

05:02.010 --> 05:04.390
would you be okay dying a little sooner 
than everyone else?

05:04.390 --> 05:06.560
Can't we drop this topic?!

05:06.560 --> 05:08.580
It won't be long before 
the folks back there—

05:08.580 --> 05:09.470
Reimi-chan.

05:09.470 --> 05:12.080
It was really scary for Akira-chan.

05:12.080 --> 05:15.950
She was so scared, 
but she still saved all of us.

05:16.550 --> 05:17.660
Oh, yeah.

05:17.660 --> 05:18.550
That's right.

05:18.550 --> 05:19.620
Sorry, Akira.

05:19.620 --> 05:20.330
It's fine.

05:20.900 --> 05:24.440
Wait, what's been going on with you 
and Pochi-san this whole time?

05:25.290 --> 05:27.320
Pochi-san keeps sniffing your butt.

05:27.320 --> 05:28.440
Did you not change your undies?

05:28.440 --> 05:28.800
Huh?!

05:28.800 --> 05:30.360
Hey, Reimi-chan!

05:31.560 --> 05:32.240
Ah.

05:32.240 --> 05:33.910
Would your underwear, perchance—

05:33.910 --> 05:34.770
Not what I meant!

05:34.770 --> 05:36.560
We did the laundry just now!

05:36.560 --> 05:38.160
Didn't you see me change?!

05:38.850 --> 05:39.840
I didn't.

05:39.840 --> 05:41.360
You didn't let anyone see you change.

05:41.360 --> 05:43.720
I hung mine to dry afterward!

05:43.720 --> 05:44.650
Oh, yeah, you did.

05:44.650 --> 05:45.580
Stupid Reimi.

05:46.240 --> 05:51.280
Episode 4       Why Are You Hiding Your Butt?

05:51.660 --> 05:54.040
We've arrived at Musashi-Yokote Station.

06:00.360 --> 06:01.680
Um...

06:01.680 --> 06:03.960
Doesn't look dangerous, at least.

06:03.960 --> 06:06.060
Doesn't look like anything, really.

06:06.060 --> 06:08.780
I'm fine as long as it's not so damp.

06:09.620 --> 06:11.040
Wait, look. A goat, a goat!

06:11.040 --> 06:14.590
Oh, yeah. Musashi-Yokote was famous 
for the goats that lived near the station.

06:14.590 --> 06:15.520
Like this one?

06:15.520 --> 06:16.660
I don't think so.

06:16.660 --> 06:17.700
It stood up!

06:17.700 --> 06:19.840
The goats in Musashi-Yokote stand on two legs?

06:19.840 --> 06:20.980
Huh, I never knew that.

06:20.980 --> 06:22.610
No, that was a question!

06:23.620 --> 06:24.590
What's it doing?

06:24.590 --> 06:26.240
Wait, is it coming this way?

06:26.240 --> 06:27.780
Yes, yes, yes it is!

06:40.010 --> 06:41.110
What <i>are</i> those things?!

06:41.110 --> 06:42.280
They look like Baphomet!

06:42.280 --> 06:43.430
You mean those are helmets?!

06:43.430 --> 06:44.240
So we can communicate?

06:44.240 --> 06:46.290
Hey, stop ramming into us!

06:48.390 --> 06:50.350
What on earth is the deal 
with those helmets?!

06:50.350 --> 06:55.640
Baphomet dates back to the 14th century, when
King Philip IV targeted the Knights Templar—

06:55.640 --> 06:56.240
Pochi-san!

06:56.240 --> 06:57.350
It's okay, don't be scared!

06:57.350 --> 06:58.050
Shizuru-chan!

06:58.050 --> 06:59.600
Faster, faster!

06:58.470 --> 06:59.940
I'm trying, okay?!

07:13.770 --> 07:16.100
What was the deal with those goats?

07:16.100 --> 07:18.100
What were they after?

07:18.100 --> 07:19.440
No clue.

07:20.160 --> 07:24.070
Are there twenty-eight more stations of <i>that</i>?

07:24.070 --> 07:24.930
Stop it.

07:24.930 --> 07:26.110
Don't say that.

07:32.440 --> 07:34.440
Take turns driving, you mean?

07:34.440 --> 07:35.090
Yes.

07:35.090 --> 07:37.180
We can't let you be the only one.

07:37.180 --> 07:37.970
Oh, yeah.

07:37.970 --> 07:41.950
I guess you <i>have</i> been driving 
ever since we left Agano.

07:41.950 --> 07:43.370
It's fine, it's fine.

07:43.370 --> 07:45.820
It was my idea to go to Ikebukuro.

07:45.820 --> 07:47.750
That doesn't matter now.

07:47.750 --> 07:48.980
I think it does.

07:48.980 --> 07:49.960
No, it doesn't.

07:49.960 --> 07:51.190
Yeah, it really doesn't.

07:51.190 --> 07:52.500
What do you think, Akira?

07:52.500 --> 07:53.210
Huh?

07:53.210 --> 07:55.730
We should all take turns driving, right?

07:56.210 --> 07:57.700
Ah, yeah.

07:57.700 --> 07:58.700
Yeah!

07:58.700 --> 07:59.810
After all...

08:01.870 --> 08:02.650
Why?

08:02.650 --> 08:03.190
Huh?

08:03.190 --> 08:04.500
Why do you think that?

08:04.500 --> 08:08.890
Well, obviously it's dangerous if she gets 
tired and falls asleep at the controls.

08:08.890 --> 08:12.830
If we take turns driving the train, 
that means more time spent moving,

08:12.830 --> 08:14.040
which makes it more efficient.

08:14.040 --> 08:16.120
We'll get to Ikebukuro faster that way.

08:16.120 --> 08:16.910
Yeah, yeah.

08:16.910 --> 08:18.720
I was thinking the same thing as Akira.

08:18.720 --> 08:20.750
See? It's all for the best.

08:21.230 --> 08:22.000
Yeah.

08:22.000 --> 08:22.680
Thanks.

08:23.130 --> 08:25.170
You need to get some rest, too.

08:25.170 --> 08:28.030
We don't know how long 
it'll be to Ikebukuro.

08:28.030 --> 08:29.580
I'm glad you're learning.

08:29.580 --> 08:31.430
You were so sure it'd only be three days.

08:31.430 --> 08:32.490
Aren't I amazing?

08:32.490 --> 08:34.450
But can you really drive this thing?

08:34.450 --> 08:35.490
I sure can!

08:35.490 --> 08:36.590
You know <i>Densha de Go</i>?

08:36.590 --> 08:38.650
I've played games like those before.

08:38.650 --> 08:40.980
Then once we finish eating 
and fold the laundry,

08:40.980 --> 08:42.480
Shizuru-chan can give us a crash course.

08:42.480 --> 08:43.230
Okay.

08:43.230 --> 08:44.820
Let's wrap up dinner real quick.

08:45.680 --> 08:48.650
I used to hate bitter melon.

08:48.650 --> 08:50.100
But it tastes good nowadays.

08:50.100 --> 08:50.790
I'm so mature now.

08:50.790 --> 08:53.960
It's even tastier eating it here like this.

08:53.960 --> 08:58.730
Now I know why Neko-nii's crew pays 
good money to buy Agano bitter melon.

08:58.730 --> 09:00.340
It may be bitter, but it's sweet, too.

09:00.340 --> 09:02.020
And it has "umami," I think it was.

09:02.020 --> 09:03.250
Oh, I know what that is.

09:03.250 --> 09:04.400
Umami, umami.

09:04.400 --> 09:08.450
Now, if I don't eat bitter melon at least 
once a day, I don't feel so great.

09:08.450 --> 09:09.740
I totally get you.

09:10.730 --> 09:11.620
What's up?

09:11.620 --> 09:12.450
Bathroom.

09:12.950 --> 09:13.860
Should I come?

09:13.860 --> 09:15.060
I'm fine by myself.

09:15.060 --> 09:16.330
Oh, have fun.

09:16.950 --> 09:19.980
If it just looked a little cuter, 
it'd be perfect.

09:25.610 --> 09:29.080
<i>If those mushrooms grow on you, 
you could die in as little as one year.</i>

09:30.250 --> 09:32.080
No way! It's fine!

09:32.080 --> 09:33.390
I'm totally fine!

09:33.390 --> 09:35.880
This is a boil, not a mushroom!

09:35.880 --> 09:38.220
I get boils really easily.

09:38.220 --> 09:39.850
Don't worry. No problem.

09:39.850 --> 09:41.590
I swear on Tatsuhiko that I'm fine!

10:20.750 --> 10:21.640
Let's get out of here!

10:21.640 --> 10:22.570
Nadeko-chan, accelerate!

10:22.570 --> 10:23.520
Ah, okay!

10:39.470 --> 10:41.870
Akira, come over here!

10:41.870 --> 10:45.070
If you don't wash yourself properly, 
Pochi-san will sniff your butt again.

10:45.070 --> 10:46.160
Shut up, moron!

10:46.160 --> 10:47.320
Flunking Reimi!

11:15.000 --> 11:17.650
Peace. Tranquility.

11:18.880 --> 11:20.990
I want to stay like this forever.

11:29.560 --> 11:32.560
Shizuru-chan, do we stop or keep going?

11:32.560 --> 11:34.480
For now, we won't stop.

11:34.480 --> 11:35.680
Let's keep moving slowly.

11:36.440 --> 11:38.930
Shizuru-chan, there are 
a ton of golf balls here.

11:38.930 --> 11:41.120
You're right. There's so many.

11:41.120 --> 11:42.120
Oh, no!

11:42.120 --> 11:42.910
What's wrong?

11:42.910 --> 11:44.650
Oh, no! Oh, no! Oh, no!

11:43.720 --> 11:45.330
Reimi-chan, you're scaring me.

11:45.330 --> 11:46.310
Just tell us.

11:46.310 --> 11:47.980
I just had an awful thought.

11:48.340 --> 11:50.830
The goat people in Musashi-Yokote Station...

11:50.830 --> 11:52.840
The weird root things at Koma Station...

11:53.270 --> 11:55.310
The golf balls here...

11:55.310 --> 11:58.300
What if the people who lived nearby...

12:03.670 --> 12:05.000
Shizuru-chan!

12:09.010 --> 12:12.080
It's raining golf ball people!

12:11.140 --> 12:13.010
No!

12:16.460 --> 12:18.760
Ugh, ew, ew, ew!

12:18.760 --> 12:20.550
What's with all these creepy stops?!

12:20.550 --> 12:22.250
Shizuru-chan, let's get this over with!

12:22.250 --> 12:24.000
That thing you said... Um, what was it?

12:24.000 --> 12:25.070
Lunch Pack?

12:25.070 --> 12:26.560
You mean "switchback."

12:25.300 --> 12:28.970
<b>Hanno</b>

12:25.300 --> 12:28.970
<b>Higashi-Hanno</b>

12:25.300 --> 12:28.970
<b>Seibu Ikebukuro Line</b>

12:25.300 --> 12:28.970
<b>Seibu Ikebukuro Line</b>

12:26.560 --> 12:28.970
Starting here, the other end will be in front.

12:28.970 --> 12:30.710
Let's move all our belongings back here.

12:30.710 --> 12:31.450
Okay.

12:31.450 --> 12:33.360
All these stops are so scary!

12:33.360 --> 12:35.220
They're just getting worse as we go.

12:35.220 --> 12:38.810
I wish we could talk to someone, 
even if they're not human, like in Agano.

12:38.810 --> 12:40.180
Don't say that.

12:40.590 --> 12:42.600
Are you gonna make fun of me again?

12:42.600 --> 12:45.120
Y'know, being able to talk...

12:45.120 --> 12:48.930
means being able to lie, 
or say hurtful things,

12:48.930 --> 12:50.940
or start arguments.

12:51.530 --> 12:54.890
If it means getting rid 
of a source of conflict,

12:54.890 --> 12:57.620
I feel like not being able to talk is fine.

12:57.620 --> 13:00.440
Then you can stay <i>real</i> still.

13:00.440 --> 13:03.350
In a dark, quiet, and damp...

13:04.130 --> 13:05.060
Huh, what?

13:05.060 --> 13:06.100
What are you doing?!

13:06.100 --> 13:07.560
Why are you hiding your butt?

13:07.560 --> 13:08.790
I'm not hiding it!

13:09.310 --> 13:10.630
Akira.

13:11.800 --> 13:12.560
Let me see!

13:12.560 --> 13:13.110
No!

13:13.110 --> 13:13.840
Show me!

13:13.840 --> 13:14.910
No way!

13:16.100 --> 13:16.930
Meanie!

13:16.930 --> 13:18.400
Like I'd give up that easily!

13:17.590 --> 13:18.610
Stop it!

13:18.610 --> 13:19.580
I'm not stopping!

13:20.100 --> 13:21.140
Let's have a look.

13:26.230 --> 13:28.490
Akira-chan, is this...

13:28.490 --> 13:29.710
No, no, no!

13:29.710 --> 13:30.480
How long have you...

13:30.480 --> 13:31.240
I'm okay!

13:31.240 --> 13:32.780
I feel totally fine!

13:32.780 --> 13:33.740
Is something wrong?

13:33.740 --> 13:35.290
Akira-chan has mushrooms growing on her!

13:35.290 --> 13:35.870
What?!

13:35.870 --> 13:37.860
I've got her, so take the other end!

13:37.860 --> 13:39.560
No, don't pull them off!

13:39.560 --> 13:41.840
I've finally achieved tranquility!

13:41.840 --> 13:42.410
You dummy!

13:42.410 --> 13:44.490
You'll die in one to two years like this!

13:44.490 --> 13:45.070
That's fine!

13:45.070 --> 13:46.730
Pessimism is cool, anyway!

13:46.730 --> 13:51.100
I don't want to live a life plagued 
with fear in this topsy-turvy world!

13:51.100 --> 13:53.210
You've always been like this!

13:53.210 --> 13:55.720
Cynical, snarky, and always 
laughing at others!

13:55.720 --> 13:56.390
Cram it!

13:56.390 --> 13:58.180
Flunking monkey Reimi!

13:58.180 --> 14:00.290
You never say anything 
when stuff happens to you

14:00.290 --> 14:02.600
and act tough even when things 
take a turn for the worse!

14:02.600 --> 14:05.060
Mushroom, mushroom, mushroom!

14:03.510 --> 14:07.400
Even though you're a scaredy-cat 
and a big crybaby!

14:17.670 --> 14:19.590
What was that?

14:20.500 --> 14:21.180
Akira!

14:21.400 --> 14:22.130
Akira!

14:22.130 --> 14:23.170
Hey, Akira!

14:23.170 --> 14:24.280
Are you okay, Akira-chan?

14:24.280 --> 14:25.420
Akira!

14:27.280 --> 14:31.030
Reimi-chan, Shizuru-chan, and Nadeko-chan.

14:31.030 --> 14:32.750
You're all so weird.

14:32.750 --> 14:35.350
Akira's doing good as always.

14:35.350 --> 14:36.950
Hunky-dory!

14:38.170 --> 14:39.300
Akira?

14:39.300 --> 14:40.390
That's me!

14:40.390 --> 14:42.390
Something's off about her.

14:42.390 --> 14:44.910
What do you mean, Nadeko-chan?

14:44.910 --> 14:46.520
Akira's not off at all!

14:46.520 --> 14:47.400
Hmph!

14:47.400 --> 14:48.480
Why?!

14:48.480 --> 14:50.620
Hmph, hmph! Hm-hm-hmph!

14:48.480 --> 14:50.730
We turned back to normal, right?!

14:50.730 --> 14:52.070
Hey, Reimi-chan!

14:52.070 --> 14:54.100
Don't yell so loud!

14:54.100 --> 14:54.610
Bad girl!

14:54.970 --> 14:58.530
Maybe the mushrooms already grew too much?

14:58.530 --> 14:59.980
They <i>were</i> really long.

14:59.980 --> 15:00.500
What?

15:00.500 --> 15:03.320
You mean we pulled out something 
we shouldn't have as well?

15:03.320 --> 15:04.630
Let's sit her up for now.

15:04.630 --> 15:05.580
C'mon, Akira.

15:05.580 --> 15:07.090
'Kay.

15:08.420 --> 15:10.540
Up I go.

15:10.540 --> 15:11.930
Huh?

15:11.930 --> 15:12.970
Oopsie.

15:12.970 --> 15:16.190
I can't move how I want.

15:16.190 --> 15:17.390
Why is that?

15:18.190 --> 15:21.280
Is this... my fault?

15:22.500 --> 15:24.550
Doesn't that feel good?

15:24.550 --> 15:26.580
Who's a cute wittle dog?

15:25.360 --> 15:28.070
Her soul. We pulled out her soul.

15:26.580 --> 15:29.570
Your face is so flabby.

15:28.070 --> 15:30.890
That irritating hipster soul of hers!

15:31.350 --> 15:32.160
No good.

15:32.160 --> 15:33.730
I don't see a hospital on here.

15:33.730 --> 15:37.050
That swan hermit's map—
I mean, scrawl—is useless!

15:37.050 --> 15:38.120
Let's go back to Agano!

15:38.120 --> 15:39.740
The water might have receded by now.

15:39.740 --> 15:41.580
No one back home can treat her.

15:41.580 --> 15:43.300
Not to mention, the tracks are all bent.

15:43.300 --> 15:46.610
Hey, what do we do if Akira ends up dying?

15:46.610 --> 15:48.350
I really don't want that to happen!

15:48.350 --> 15:50.250
Calm down. It'll be fine.

15:50.250 --> 15:50.930
Yeah.

15:50.930 --> 15:52.900
I'm sure we'll be able to fix her, Reimi-chan.

15:52.900 --> 15:53.470
Okay?

15:53.760 --> 15:55.920
But I was the one who...

15:57.110 --> 16:00.920
Starting today, I'm going 
to call you Anthony!

16:03.680 --> 16:06.350
Please, Zenjiro-san, help us somehow!

16:06.350 --> 16:09.650
I'll stop calling you a stupid old fart, 
no matter what you do from now on!

16:09.650 --> 16:10.760
What?!

16:10.760 --> 16:13.450
That sounds like it's 
affected her brain directly!

16:13.450 --> 16:14.300
I've got this!

16:14.300 --> 16:15.740
If you're in Hanno...

16:15.740 --> 16:19.560
"I know a good doctor with a foul mouth."

16:19.560 --> 16:22.570
"Used to be colleagues."

16:22.570 --> 16:27.270
"In grade school, 
pooped pants and blamed me."

16:27.270 --> 16:33.100
"Cheated on test, recorder saliva incident, 
blamed me for everything."

16:33.100 --> 16:36.340
"Now in Inariyama Parchoo-choo choo-choo..."

16:39.680 --> 16:42.030
Stupid old fart!

16:40.780 --> 16:42.410
Inariyama...

16:42.410 --> 16:44.590
Does he mean Inariyama Park?

16:44.590 --> 16:46.110
Yeah, I think so.

16:46.110 --> 16:47.730
Ah, the poop that tastes like curry!

16:47.730 --> 16:49.580
We've had enough poop talk for one day!

16:49.580 --> 16:50.350
No, no.

16:50.350 --> 16:51.720
Akira mentioned it back then!

16:52.450 --> 16:56.000
Kazuyo-san said there's a good doctor 
in Inariyama Park.

16:56.000 --> 16:56.490
Really?!

16:56.490 --> 16:58.090
Kazuyo-san, the capybara?

16:58.090 --> 16:58.830
Yeah.

16:58.830 --> 17:01.220
But they don't know who it is 
or if they're human.

17:01.220 --> 17:05.710
We don't even know what 
Inariyama Park looks like nowadays.

17:05.710 --> 17:07.020
Don't panic.

17:07.020 --> 17:07.920
Calm down.

17:10.530 --> 17:13.870
We'll head there, steadily but quickly.

17:24.190 --> 17:25.920
Shizuru-chan.

17:26.490 --> 17:28.610
How's it look, Shizuru-chan?

17:28.610 --> 17:32.190
Well, I didn't see anyone!

17:32.190 --> 17:34.820
But you can use the bathrooms here.

17:34.820 --> 17:36.320
They have running water.

17:36.320 --> 17:38.010
I might go as well, then.

17:38.010 --> 17:39.220
Me too.

17:39.220 --> 17:40.210
Shizuru-chan.

17:40.210 --> 17:41.240
Yeah, okay.

17:41.240 --> 17:42.370
I'll look after Akira.

17:42.370 --> 17:43.190
Thanks.

17:43.450 --> 17:45.200
Finally, someone who can talk!

17:45.200 --> 17:46.300
Well, duh!

17:46.300 --> 17:47.440
I'm a jizo, dang it!

17:47.440 --> 17:49.200
What's Inariyama Park like?

17:49.200 --> 17:50.780
Is there a human doctor there?

17:50.780 --> 17:52.310
Don't ask me!

17:52.310 --> 17:54.030
We can't move, you know.

17:54.030 --> 17:56.790
That said, it's real nice not having 
to move once you get used to it.

17:57.030 --> 18:00.340
Ticks me off that I can't eat 
these offerings, though.

18:00.340 --> 18:03.400
Inariyama-koen Station is 
two stops from here, right?

18:03.400 --> 18:04.770
That's all I know.

18:04.770 --> 18:06.000
Dunno about any doctors.

18:06.000 --> 18:07.060
Sorry.

18:07.060 --> 18:08.150
<b>Irumashi</b>

18:23.070 --> 18:26.780
Innards. Innards.

18:27.340 --> 18:29.410
Innards.

18:40.810 --> 18:42.180
Okay, Nadeko-chan.

18:42.180 --> 18:43.360
Take care of Akira.

18:43.360 --> 18:43.840
Sure.

18:43.840 --> 18:45.720
Shizuru-chan, take care of Reimi-chan.

18:45.720 --> 18:46.700
Yeah, okay.

18:46.700 --> 18:48.560
Why do I need taking care of?

18:48.560 --> 18:51.530
You sometimes lose sight of the big picture.

18:51.530 --> 18:53.650
Huh? Who, me?

18:53.650 --> 18:55.180
Don't know what you mean.

19:02.440 --> 19:03.870
Hey, there's nothing here!

19:03.870 --> 19:05.120
For real.

19:05.120 --> 19:07.460
Not a soul in sight, doctor or otherwise.

19:09.400 --> 19:11.270
Something's ringing.

19:12.030 --> 19:12.830
That way!

19:13.340 --> 19:15.450
Hmm, I see something.

19:15.450 --> 19:16.970
Looks like a wall.

19:16.970 --> 19:18.800
No way... I don't see anything.

19:18.800 --> 19:21.170
You really <i>do</i> have a vision of 25.

19:21.170 --> 19:23.420
No, it's only 2.5.

19:25.000 --> 19:25.980
It stopped.

19:25.980 --> 19:26.780
Let's check it out.

19:27.480 --> 19:29.980
Shizuru-chan! Look, a town!

19:30.590 --> 19:32.370
Looks empty, though.

19:32.370 --> 19:34.730
There was that weird ringing just now, though.

19:34.730 --> 19:35.520
Yeah, I heard it.

19:35.520 --> 19:37.610
A person must have set it off.

19:37.610 --> 19:40.060
Let's circle around and scope things—

19:39.440 --> 19:41.210
No, we don't have much time.

19:41.620 --> 19:44.780
We need to find a doctor quick 
and have them look at Akira.

19:49.240 --> 19:50.370
So close!

19:50.370 --> 19:52.000
More like small!

19:52.000 --> 19:53.880
What is this? Are we Gulliver?

19:53.880 --> 19:55.710
This is kind of cute.

19:55.710 --> 19:57.620
It's like we're at whatsit World Square.

19:57.620 --> 20:00.060
I think everything was smaller there.

20:00.060 --> 20:02.480
I guess there really is no one here.

20:02.480 --> 20:03.950
Looks like it.

20:07.890 --> 20:08.940
A plane?!

20:08.940 --> 20:11.020
Wow, haven't seen <i>that</i> in a while!

20:18.260 --> 20:20.520
Ow, ow, ow!

20:19.550 --> 20:20.750
What? What?

20:20.750 --> 20:21.500
That hurts!

20:21.500 --> 20:23.360
Actually, it's more itchy than painful!

20:23.360 --> 20:24.200
Oh, you're right.

20:24.200 --> 20:25.650
Man, I'm itchy!

20:25.650 --> 20:28.480
Ow! Itchy! Ow! Itchy!

20:28.480 --> 20:29.460
Over here!

20:32.990 --> 20:34.190
No way...

20:34.190 --> 20:35.800
Toy soldiers!

20:39.090 --> 20:42.030
Ow! Itchy! Ow! Itchy!

20:44.420 --> 20:45.180
What?!

20:45.180 --> 20:46.580
How many <i>are</i> there?!

20:46.010 --> 20:48.090
Hey, we're not here to...

20:50.480 --> 20:55.440
Ow! Itchy! Ow! Itchy!

21:01.760 --> 21:03.860
A-Akira...

21:07.670 --> 21:08.740
Akira!

21:09.290 --> 21:11.250
Akira, wait!

21:13.890 --> 21:16.000
I finally caught up!

21:16.000 --> 21:16.760
What's wrong?

21:16.750 --> 21:20.750
<b>Iron Monty's
Splendid Wednesday</b>

21:16.760 --> 21:20.750
I have no idea how to study 
for tomorrow's Japanese test!

21:20.750 --> 21:22.820
Tell me how I can get a good score!

21:22.820 --> 21:25.750
If I did that, you'd stop 
being Flunking Reimi.

21:25.750 --> 21:27.160
I'm fine with that!

21:27.160 --> 21:28.770
I <i>want</i> to stop!

21:29.570 --> 21:33.600
Tear out the parts you want to memorize 
from a textbook or dictionary, put them

21:33.600 --> 21:35.440
between two Togo rice crackers, and eat it.

21:35.440 --> 21:37.940
Wow! You're so smart, Akira!

21:46.280 --> 21:50.360
Ow, ow, ow, ow!

21:55.420 --> 21:56.800
Ow...

22:01.630 --> 22:02.180
Eh?

22:03.760 --> 22:08.020
What the hell?!
